# Example environment file for Mylonite.
#
# Mylonite ships with NO default LLM provider. You must configure one before
# any command that calls an LLM (`scan`, `generate`, `validate`, `gate`,
# `ablate`). All LLM calls go through LiteLLM, so any LiteLLM-supported
# provider works.
#
# Anthropic and OpenAI are both first-class targets. You can keep keys for
# more than one provider in this file; the model prefix (or --provider, or
# MYLONITE_MODEL below) decides which is *used* for a given run, so swapping
# is a one-variable change. Do not commit your real .env file — see .gitignore.
#
# `mylonite --env-file <path>` loads exactly the variables named in this file:
# recognised provider credentials/config plus the MYLONITE_* settings below.
# Anything else is ignored and reported on stderr, so a .env reused from a wider
# project cannot inject arbitrary environment into a Mylonite run.

# Pick the active model (required before any LLM call) -- lowest-precedence
# source, below an explicit --model flag or a mylonite.yaml `model:` entry.
# Prefix with the provider (LiteLLM convention) when it isn't Anthropic.
# MYLONITE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6
# MYLONITE_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o

# Role-separated models (each defaults to MYLONITE_MODEL when unset) --
# see `mylonite scan --help` for --planner-model/--customiser-model/--judge-model.
# MYLONITE_PLANNER_MODEL=
# MYLONITE_CUSTOMISER_MODEL=
# MYLONITE_JUDGE_MODEL=

# Self-hosted/proxy endpoint (Ollama, vLLM, a corporate LiteLLM proxy/gateway).
# MUST be credential-free -- Mylonite refuses a userinfo (user:pass@host) or a
# key-shaped query param (?api_key=...) here; put the credential in its own
# env var (e.g. one of the provider keys below, or your proxy's own).
# MYLONITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:11434

# Per-call tuning (all optional; defaults documented in
# mylonite.scan.llm_policy.LLMPolicy).
# MYLONITE_MAX_TOKENS=2048
# MYLONITE_TEMPERATURE=0.0
# MYLONITE_TIMEOUT=120
# MYLONITE_NUM_RETRIES=2

# Anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# OpenAI
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Azure OpenAI
# AZURE_API_KEY=
# AZURE_API_BASE=
# AZURE_API_VERSION=

# AWS Bedrock (uses standard AWS credentials chain)
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_REGION_NAME=

# Local model server (e.g. Ollama, vLLM, LM Studio)
# OPENAI_API_BASE=http://localhost:11434/v1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=not-needed
